  "notes": [
    "## Event to field reasoning - Pending Reservation Confirmations\n\nThis is a **todo-list read model** (`todoListElement: true`) feeding the `Reservation Confirmation Mailer` automation, not a screen.\n\n- **Reservation Placed** -> opens the todo item. Sets `Id`, `RestaurantId`, `Email` - everything the Mailer needs to send the confirmation. The reservation does not need a confirmation before this event exists.\n- **Reservation Confirmation Sent** -> closes the todo item (removes the row). This is the backward `EVENT -> READMODEL` edge the platform allows specifically because this read model already has a `READMODEL -> AUTOMATION` edge - the todo-list accumulator exception. No field changes value; the row simply leaves the set once the confirmation is sent.\n\n### Why this enforces \"sent only once\"\n\nThe automation only ever acts on rows still open in this list. Once `Reservation Confirmation Sent` closes the item, the Mailer has nothing left to act on for that reservation - the guarantee is structural, not a check the automation has to remember to make. The command-level `Confirmation Cannot Be Sent Twice` scenario on `Send Reservation Confirmation` asserts the same guarantee as defense in depth, in case the command is ever invoked directly outside the automation's own read loop.\n\n### Fan-in\n\nTwo connected events, one opening and one closing the same item - the expected shape for a todo list, not a violation of the >3-events heuristic."
